": 62, "color": "W", "move": "pass", "lead_before": -21.95, "lead_after": -22.0, "points_lost": -0.05, "best": "G8"}], "review": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "title": "A Seesaw Through the Endgame, Then a Slide", "summary": "The 14k won as White by 22 points after two passes. The game was close until Opus 5.5 lost 10.1 points at move 17, and from there the lead swung back and forth through the 30s, with both sides giving away 13 to 22 points a move. The last swings went White's way: A8 at move 41 and F8 at move 43 left Black at -21.9 with nothing more to play for. Opus 5.5 averaged 5.8 points lost per move and the 14k 5.0, so the result came down to which side made the final big loss.", "moments": [{"turn": 17, "text": "C7 extended Black's left-hand wall but lost 10.1 points, dropping Black's lead from -4.3 to -14.5. The engine preferred D3. It was the largest single drop so far in a game that had been within a couple of points for most of the opening."}, {"turn": 28, "text": "E4 was a gift. The 14k lost 9.8 points with it and Black's lead went from -9.5 to +0.2, with G8 the engine's choice. Opus 5.5 was behind for the first time since move 8 and then ahead on the board, and it did not hold the lead."}, {"turn": 36, "text": "After Opus 5.5 played B8 and fell to -19.7, the 14k played B9 and lost 22.1 points, bringing the lead back to +2.4. Neither side was converting a lead here, since each big mistake was answered by an equally big one."}, {"turn": 41, "text": "A8 was the worst move of the game for Opus 5.5, losing 26.0 points and turning a +4.3 lead into -21.7. The engine wanted H9 on the open upper right, and Black played on the left edge instead."}, {"turn": 43, "text": "F8 lost another 21.9 points, taking the lead from +0.0 to -21.9, again with H9 as the engine's choice. The 14k answered with H9 itself at move 44 and the lead stayed near -22 to the end, so this was where the game was decided."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py only